</section></score></mdiv></body>
<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>They know, who thus oppress me,</l><l>’Tis hard to be alone;</l><l>But know not One can bless me,</l><l>Who comes through bars and stone;</l><l>He makes my dungeon’s darkness bright,</l><l>And fills my bosom with delight.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Thy love, O God, restores me</l><l>From sighs and tears to praise;</l><l>And deep my soul adores Thee,</l><l>Nor thinks of time or place:</l><l>I ask no more, in good or ill,</l><l>But union with Thy holy will.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>’Tis that which makes my treasure,</l><l>’Tis that which brings my gain;</l><l>Converting woe to pleasure,</l><l>And reaping joy from pain.</l><l>Oh, ’tis enough, whate’er befall,</l><l>To know that God is All in all.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
